From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:07:19 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 100/148] hjviewer: back closes HJViewer's dialogs as their
 cancel does, and goes home from a phone tab
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

UX-M2, the call sites:
- U63: A1 and A2 (a refused session) pass their [취소] and [닫기] as onBack, so a back press
  also closes the session as the button does, and while A1 checks the access password. P2, P3,
  S2, the main window's close question (back keeps the window open), the account screens'
  dialogs, the relogin notice and the update screens close on back, as their only cancel is the
  dialog's close; the new-device notice, which waits for an answer, keeps swallowing it. The
  login dialog passes its close (onDialogCancel). Upstream dialogs are unchanged.
- The phone home's WillPopScope becomes a PopScope: back on another tab goes to the first tab,
  on it the app goes back, as before. The manifest keeps predictive back off (U60, 1.8.2) until
  an Android 16 device passes every back path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
